            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Oxalis exilis, the least yellow sorrel or shady woodsorrel, is a small herbaceous plant found in Australia and New Zealand.{{r|plantnet|wa|edible}} It is mainly found in hillsides and weedy areas. It is the smallest species of Oxalis in New Zealand.{{r|sykes2009}} The colors of the leaves range from green to purple. The capsule and style length vary from 4–6.5 mm.{{r|sykes2009}}"
